{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>אֵלֶּה תוֹלְדוֹת הַשָּׁמַיִם וְהָאָרֶץ בְּהִבָּרְאָם.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory said in the Midrash (Menachot 29b): בְּהֵ״א בְּרָאָם — with a ה he created them, for this world was created with a ה and the world to come with a י. And it appears that the intent of the author of this midrash is that all the songs of this world were uttered in the feminine mode — שִׁירָה חֲדָשָׁה with the addition of a ה — for every ה indicates the feminine, as in the indication of the ה in the word אִשָּׁה, and because all the joy of this world is mixed with pain and grief, like a woman who has pain of childbirth, so too all the matters of this world are in the manner of genesis (תּוֹלָדָה). But the world to come was created with a י, which is joined to the masculine, who has no pain of childbirth; so too the world to come will be like males who do not give birth, and there joy is complete. Therefore the name י-ה was joined between man (אִישׁ) and woman (אִשָּׁה), and everywhere the function of the י is for the masculine and the function of the ה for the feminine." "<b>בְּיוֹם עֲשׂוֹת ה׳ אֱלֹהִים אֶרֶץ וְשָׁמָיִם.</b> And above he put the heavens before the earth, because our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Rashi here 1:1, Bereshit Rabbah 12:15): the Holy One, blessed be He, wished to create the world with the attribute of justice, and saw that it could not endure — so He went back and joined to it the attribute of mercy. But behold, 'He is not a man that He should relent' — and from the outset, what did He think? Rather, in truth the heavens and all their spiritual hosts can endure under the attribute of justice more than the lower beings whose foundation is in dust. Therefore this one is placed adjacent to this and this one adjacent to this: for above he mentioned the name Elohim and attached it to ״אֵת הַשָּׁמַיִם״ — that multiplies all their host — for they were created under the attribute of justice alone. And here he mentioned the joining of mercy and attached it to the earth, for the sake of the inhabitants of the earth this joining was necessary. And concerning this joining the psalmist said (Psalms 62:12): ״אַחַת דִּבֶּר אֱלֹהִים שְׁתַּיִם זוּ שָׁמַעְתִּי״ etc. — for at first ״אַחַת דִּבֶּר אֱלֹהִים״, that is, one attribute was mentioned with the name Elohim, when He said ״בְּרֵאשִׁית בָּרָא אֱלֹהִים״, and afterwards ״שְׁתַּיִם זוּ שָׁמַעְתִּי״ etc. — two attributes, when He said ״בְּיוֹם עֲשׂוֹת ה׳ אֱלֹהִים״. A hint to the matter: ״שְׁתַּיִם זוּ״ yields the number twenty-six, equal to the number of the name of mercy, and He divided it into twice thirteen, equal to the number of ״אֶחָד״ and ״אַהֲבָה״, which are included in the name of mercy and which are adjacent to each other in the verse ״שְׁמַע יִשְׂרָאֵל״ etc. ״ה׳ אֶחָד״, ״וְאָהַבְתָּ״ etc. (Deuteronomy 6:4–5). And He gave a reason for the matter, why He did not create it with the name Elohim alone: ״כִּי עֹז לֵאלֹהִים״ — for all might and strength is attributed to the name Elohim, and there is no power in the hands of created beings below to withstand every act of His strength and might, blessed be He, at all. But ״לְךָ ה׳ חָסֶד״ — for to the name of mercy, which is called by the name of Adonai, belong kindness and mercy; for a time will come when He will wish to repay a man according to his deed in accordance with the capacity of the recipient and the doer, not according to His own power, blessed be He. And He used the language of direct address in saying ״וּלְךָ ה׳ חָסֶד״, and the language of concealment with the name Elohim, ״כִּי עֹז לֵאלֹהִים״ — for at the time of anger, when the attribute of justice holds sway in the world, it appears as though HaShem hid His face from the creatures, and at the time of kindness and mercy HaShem illuminates His face toward us — and it is easy to understand."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {1 "The verse ״כִּי עֹז לֵאלֹהִים״ is from Psalms 62:12, continuing the same verse already cited above (אַחַת דִבֶּר אֱלֹהִים שְׁתַּיִם זוּ שָׁמַעְתִּי), as is ״לְךָ ה׳ חָסֶד״ from the same verse; the Kli Yakar does not cite these addresses separately."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:27:00.197810818Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}